From 4860ee05a9ac1a5b77cce08d9b6b44b5358ebd40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:34:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): keep a slow-but-alive SSH backend instead of
 reconnecting it in a loop [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On 2026-11-12 the MacBook sat on a ~60-175 KB/s network. The tunnel to the hub was alive, but the 10 s dispatch
/api/health probe timed out, the pooled backend was retired, its SSH master torn down, and the reconnect refetched
everything over the same link, so the next probe timed out too: "failed its dispatch probe ... reconnecting on
demand" every 1-2 minutes for an hour while a trivial command through the tunnel took 34 s.

- remote-liveness: a dispatch probe that TIMES OUT while the SSH master is alive keeps the descriptor (slow, not
  down). Refused/reset/hang-up, a dead master, or 3 timeouts with no answer in between still retire it.
- slow-link.ts: per-backend slow state. Entered only by that live-transport probe timeout (answer times alone
  never enter it); left when the median of the last 5 answers is under 1 s, or after 10 min without slow
  evidence; cleared whenever the pooled descriptor is dropped (stopPoolBackend). While slow:
  fetchJsonForBackend stretches every request and probe timeout x4 (cap 60 s); the timer-polled paths
  (/api/plugins/*, /api/session-kanban-tasks) run one per scope and path at most every 30 s, the rest failing as
  a quiet PowerSettlingError (user-driven reads such as opening a session are never thinned, and a poll that
  never reached the wire frees its slot); the transcript prefetch pass skips that connection.
- ssh-connection: Compression=yes on Desktop's own ssh options (the traffic is almost all JSON).

Known cost: `ssh -O check` proves the master process, not the link. After a silent network drop the master lives
until its keepalive gives up (~45 s), and for that window requests wait their stretched timeout instead of
failing after the 10 s probe.

Not in this change: the renderer still says "Reconnecting to Hermes…" when its WebSocket is down (a "slow
connection" indicator is a follow-up), and the three background revalidation paths get the stretched timeouts but
no live-transport tolerance.

Tests: slow-link.test.ts (tracker entry/exit/expiry/strikes, poll thinning per scope, session opens never
thinned, unsent poll frees its slot, a backend answering after 12 s is kept and a 4 s request then fits, three
probe timeouts end to end retire it, held error carries the renderer guard's marker, main.ts wiring pinned by
source text), remote-liveness.test.ts (kept when alive; retired when dead, refused, reset, hung up, the transport
check throws, or given up), transcript-prefetch.test.ts (paused connection skipped, resumes),
ssh-connection.test.ts (Compression=yes). main.ts is over its line cap, so its wiring lives in slow-link.ts
(dispatchSlowLink, thinnedPoll, noteRemoteAnswer; the remote-timing first-request helper moved with it) and those
helpers are executed by tests; the remaining call sites in main.ts are pinned by source text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
